Host-side project tests (no hardware required, run from the project root):

- node test/decoder.test.js
    Decoder regression tests for chirpstack/decoder.js: CayenneLPP metric and
    imperial (rain/pressure resolution), debug channels (Generic Sensor and
    legacy Analog Input), binary version 1 (older firmware) and unknown
    versions.

- node test/payload_roundtrip.test.js
    Compiles src/payload_binary.cpp together with test/payload_roundtrip.cpp
    for the host (c++/g++/clang++, CXX overrides; skipped if none is found),
    encodes known measurement sets (metric, imperial, minimal, out of range,
    PCB v2.0 I/O block incl. VE.Direct)
    and checks that decoder.js returns the same values - and clamps instead
    of wrapping.

- node test/vedirect.test.js
    Compiles src/vedirect.cpp with test/vedirect_parser.cpp for the host and
    feeds it Victron VE.Direct text-protocol streams: MPPT and BMV blocks,
    corrupt checksums, interleaved HEX messages, a mid-stream start and
    "---" values.

- node test/firmware_runtime.test.js
    Compiles the real sensors, board I/O, parameter, JSON and LoRa transport
    modules with deterministic hardware fakes. Exercises stuck/recovered
    1-Wire conversions, output/PWM shutdown, battery hysteresis and missing
    VE.Direct/PV data, standalone wind 2, energy-setting save/read-back,
    bounded radio/join retries, node cleanup, timer rollover and JSON >1024
    bytes, rain statistics bookkeeping (ISO weeks, period roll-over,
    today/yesterday/last rain, NVS blob v2 round trip and migration of the
    old 28-byte blob, power loss and planned-restart flush with the NVS
    copy, rain before the clock sync, at most 25 flash writes per day incl.
    restarts, none with the setting off), VPD, the new-node
    defaults, the wireless "Auto (search)" rotation/lock decision and the
    Loxone UDP lines (names, 0/1 booleans, flattened nested values, prefix,
    invalid/stale values left out, decimals, settings sanitizing).
    Requires a C++11 compiler and the ArduinoJson dependency restored
    by the normal PlatformIO build. Does not flash or simulate physical timing.

- node test/pcb_protection.test.js
    Checks PCB v2.0 against tools/pcbgen/design.py: VIN/USB disconnect (J3,
    JP8), fan high-side switch and gate resistor bank, sensor-rail LDO (U7,
    F3, C35), footprints, nets, fixed positions, silkscreen notes, the SMD BOM
    (47 lines / 135 references), the THT list (8 lines / 22 references) and
    the fan PWM stability results. Requires python3.

- node test/pcb_cpl.test.js
    Rebuilds the JLCPCB CPL with tools/pcbgen/jlcpcb_cpl.py from the board
    angles and checks it equals the committed CPL: 135 placements, preview-
    matched rotation offsets, Q7 centroid 1.4 mm towards the leads, all other
    positions unchanged, plus the article/angle guards. Requires python3.

- node test/api_contract.test.js
    Compiles json_payload.cpp, history.cpp and api_info.cpp with
    test/firmware_api.cpp (five deterministic fixtures: Bresser 7-in-1 +
    BME280, Ecowitt WS90/WH31/WH51/WH57, PCB v2.0 fully equipped, imperial,
    Heltec V4 after boot) and checks /api/data, /api/history and /api/info:
    equal to docs/api/examples/ (numbers within 1e-4), valid against
    docs/api/schemas/ (validator: test/json_schema_lite.js), every emitted
    key described in a schema, every schema property described, no secret
    in any document. Regenerate the examples after an intended change:
    UPDATE_API_EXAMPLES=1 node --test test/api_contract.test.js
    Requires a C++11 compiler and ArduinoJson from the PlatformIO build.

- node test/doc_links.test.js
    Every relative link, image and #anchor (GitHub heading ids) in the
    project's Markdown files (git-tracked and new, without lib/) resolves.

Run all scripts together: node --test test/*.test.js

These are plain Node.js scripts, not PlatformIO unit tests; `pio test` is
not used in this project.
